    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nNeovim uses 1-2% CPU when a picker is open, even when it's not receiving any input. It would ideally idle or use less CPU.\n\nFor comparison:\n- fzf uses some CPU, but significantly less\n- The Helix editor appears to be completely idle when a picker is open\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- Open `nvim`\n- Check process monitor and confirm `nvim` CPU is 0%\n- Open any picker\n- Check process monitor and confirm `nvim` CPU usage is 1-2%\n  - `strace` shows non-stop `epoll_pwait()` in the `nvim --embed` process\n- Stop picker\n- Check process monitor and confirm `nvim` CPU is 0%\n\nI can reproduce this on both Linux and macOS.",
