        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I set `config.delay.async = 1000` and the CPU usage is basically negligible now, and as you mentioned I haven't noticed any negative effects on the picker (or Neovim itself).\n\nThank you!\n\n> The default 10 ms is chosen for a smooth default experience since 1-2% CPU load for something that is called on demand and is not very long lived seems acceptable.\n\nFWIW, this is a surprising default to me. A picker is usually short lived, but not always - I could see myself switching to another program with a picker open and leaving it there for hours (potentially days). This might impact battery life.\n\nI have a quiet Neovim setup and definitely don't need ~100 screen redraws per second. I had to to run `while true; date; sleep 0.01; end` in a `:terminal` to notice any difference.",
