        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I'll think about maybe changing it to 100 ms, though.\n\nI suspect that would be a better compromise.\n\nSomewhat related: I also just realized that the output from `while true; date; sleep 0.01; end` in Neovim `:terminal` completely freezes the moment you enter into command mode with `:`. I'm not sure if that's the case for regular buffer updates as well. Vim 9.1 does not have this terminal output freezing problem.\n\nI think ideally there would be an API similar to `getcharstr()` that doesn't block redraws to make it possible to achieve Helix-like performance.\n\nThank you again for the support and for sharing this amazing project with us.",
