            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Okay, so after a lot of internal back-and-forth, I decided to remove this constant forcing of redraw whenever `getcharstr()` waits for the input. The behavior of not redrawing seems to be more aligned with other modes (like Command-line mode) and the only issue I had with \"background drawing\" was 'mini.notify' which works.\n\nThe currently only user-facing bad side effect is that async highlighting inside preview (like after `vim.treesitter.start()`) will no longer be visible immediately. It is fixed by forcing redraw only once per preview, which is much better than constant indefinite one. And this problem only showed up only in `builtin.help` picker, though, so hopefully will not be a big problem.\n\n@justinmayhew, so it should be now safe for you to remove adjusting `config.delay.async`.",
